From: Razoc <razoc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:13:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 37/51] feat(akibot): in-game menu on F1 / Escape with the
 launcher's options

New AkiBotMenu (src/graphics/presentation/akibotMenu.*), shown through the
system overlay as a new OverlayKind::Menu: it captures the controller,
keyboard and mouse while open, so the game gets no input.

- Every option of the AkiBot launcher, read from and saved to the file
  named by AKIBOT_SETTINGS_FILE (same JSON keys and values), texts in
  French or English (AKIBOT_LANG).
- Applied at once: frame-rate limit (VideoOut::SetFrameLimit), FPS
  counter (SetPerformanceOverlayMode), fullscreen, game speed
  (VideoOut::SetGameSpeedPercent). The others are marked "*" and apply
  on the next start.
- Keyboard: arrows, Enter/Space, Page Up/Down or Q/E/Tab for tabs,
  Escape or F1 to close. Controller: D-pad, A, B, LB/RB, Start.
- F1 no longer triggers a RenderDoc capture (now Ctrl+F1). Escape stays
  with a system dialog or the on-screen keyboard when one is shown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
